WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.120
Oberyn Martell: "Unbowed, Unbent, Unbroken."&nbsp;
The words of House Martell.A promise to our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.880
enemies and a challenge to our lovers.
Thousands of years ago, the warrior queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.960
Nymeria crossed into Dorne from Essos, fleeing&nbsp;
the dragonlords of Valyria. After she landed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.480
she burned her ships, all ten thousand&nbsp;
of them, so no cowards could slink home.
&nbsp;

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.480
What a woman. Dornish in spirit&nbsp;
before she ever was in flesh.
&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.360
She was lucky to land in Dorne, where powerful&nbsp;
women are not locked away in septs and the beds of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:44.720
old men. My ancestor, Mors Martell, saw her and&nbsp;
desired her, and proved that where armies fail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.800
a tongue may succeed.
Wedding his strength to hers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:55.200
his spear to her sun, they subdued&nbsp;
all of his rivals together. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.160
the tradition of her people, House Martell&nbsp;
then ruled Dorne as Princes, not kings.
&nbsp;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:06.800
Twice the Targaryens tried to conquer&nbsp;
Dorne with soldiers. Twice they failed.
&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.640
Only when the dragon kings came bearing husbands&nbsp;
and wives did my ancestors relent and agree&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:18.560
to join their Seven Kingdoms. House Martell&nbsp;
could have waged war until the end of days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.400
but how could we resist a&nbsp;
peace we could take to bed?
&nbsp;

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:29.920
Eventually, after centuries of courtship, House&nbsp;
Martell got into bed with the Targaryens. We took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.800
King Daeron II and his sister for our&nbsp;
own before they could take each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.840
and six kingdoms became seven.
Even now, I do not blame my ancestors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:46.480
One look at those long silver locks. It is&nbsp;
not every day a man gets to ride a dragon.
&nbsp;

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.320
But they soon learned that you can't&nbsp;
leap off a dragon at will. My sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:58.000
Elia. She married Prince Rhaegar Targaryen&nbsp;
and became the Princess she already was.
&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.400
In Dorne, she walked among vipers, and&nbsp;
none would bite her. In King's Landing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.440
she found herself surrounded by lions.
When Robert Baratheon rebelled against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.280
his rightful king, his future&nbsp;
father-in-law, Tywin Lannister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:19.360
ordered his beast Gregor Clegane to murder my&nbsp;
sister along with her helpless children.
&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.680
And men call the Lannisters "heroes."
Viserys Targaryen: After the submission of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:31.120
House Stark, Aegon marches towards Oldtown,&nbsp;
steeling himself for another battle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:38.320
But he found the gates open, with the&nbsp;
High Septon welcoming him. The pious fool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:44.800
even had the arrogance to grant what Aegon had&nbsp;
already won, and anointed the last Valyrian as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:51.760
"Aegon of House Targaryen, First of His Name,&nbsp;
King of the Andals and the First Men, Lord of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:58.720
Seven Kingdoms and Protector of the Realm." 
Varys: But while Aegon titled himself Lord of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:04.160
the Seven Kingdoms, in reality,&nbsp;
he held only six. The seventh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:10.240
Dorne, had never knelt. Visenya had flown&nbsp;
into the Vale and returned with its crown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:16.560
Mimicking her sister, Rhaenys had flown over&nbsp;
the enemy force holding the passes into Dorne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.960
and landed in the castle of its ruling&nbsp;
lady, Princess Meria of House Martell.
&nbsp;

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:27.440
Meria was eighty years old, fat,&nbsp;
bald, and blind. Behind her back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.640
many sniggered at her as the "Yellow Toad&nbsp;
of Dorne." The beautiful Rhaenys probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.520
thought as much when they met. She demanded&nbsp;
Princess Meria kneel to her brother Aegon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.800
though she allowed that on account of Meria's age&nbsp;
and health, a simple vow of submission would do.
&nbsp;

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.080
But the princess told the queen that&nbsp;
the Targaryens weren't wanted in Dorne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.560
and no Martell would ever bow, bend or&nbsp;
break no matter how badly they burned.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.880
Rhaenys could have mounted her dragon right then,&nbsp;
and roasted Meria in the castle as her brother had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:05.440
done at Harrenhal. But whatever she saw in Meria's&nbsp;
eyes scared her right back to King's Landing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.600
with a dragon's tail between its legs.
&nbsp;

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:13.840
After Aegon's coronation, Rhaenys&nbsp;
returned to Dorne with Aegon and Visenya&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.560
and their dragons. But no armies met them in the&nbsp;
field, and no lords defied them in their castles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:28.240
As the dragons approached, Dorne simply emptied.&nbsp;
House Martell had learned from Harrenhal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:34.000
and the Field of Fire. The dragons were unbeatable&nbsp;
in battle, but wars were more than battles.
&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:40.240
Unopposed, Aegon claimed Dorne for his own.&nbsp;
But as soon as he returned to King's Landing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:46.000
his castellans were hurled off towers, and his&nbsp;
royal garrison vanished in the desert, never to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:52.320
seen again. Except, perhaps, when the winds change&nbsp;
and the sands cough up old bones and armor.Rhaenys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:58.000
returned on Meraxes, intent&nbsp;
on avenging herself against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:05.840
Meria Martell. But Dorne was no longer empty.&nbsp;
The Dornish kept Meria's promise and fought even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:13.520
while burning under dragon flame. And they won.
One day a bolt pierced the eye of Meraxes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:20.640
knocked the dragon out of the sky. House Martell&nbsp;
remained unbroken, unlike the unfortunate Rhaenys.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:27.360
In their wrath, Aegon and Visenya set flame to&nbsp;
every castle and city but Sunspear, trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:33.360
turn the people against House Martell. But the&nbsp;
Dornish stayed loyal, and when Aegon returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:37.840
to King's Landing, he found assassins waiting&nbsp;
for him in the streets of his own capital.
&nbsp;

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:42.800
If not for Visenya, the Conqueror would not&nbsp;
have enjoyed his conquest for very long.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:48.560
From then on, the king and his family would&nbsp;
be guarded by the seven greatest knights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:54.000
in the realm: the Kingsguard.
When Meria died in her sleep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:00.080
a weak and tired son sued for peace. But&nbsp;
old Meria had exhausted Aegon as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:06.480
and he granted the request. The Targaryens still&nbsp;
wanted Dorne, and eventually, they would have it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:11.680
but not at the point of a sword. They would&nbsp;
buy it the same way great lords buy anything:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.920
with a daughter.
Ellaria Sand: Before the Seven Kingdoms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:23.200
before the Iron Throne, there was Dorne.&nbsp;
Twelve thousand years ago, the First Men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:29.040
crossed the land bridge from Essos to here. Of&nbsp;
course, they were men, so they soon broke it.
&nbsp;

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:35.920
Then, while their cousins to the North built&nbsp;
kingdoms, the Dornish squabbled over land, water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:44.640
and wives for centuries. Until&nbsp;
Nymeria, a warrior princess in Essos.
&nbsp;

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:48.240
She led a fleet of ten thousand&nbsp;
ships across the Narrow Sea to Dorne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:52.480
Almost all of the petty lords made&nbsp;
it clear that she wasn't welcome.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.440 --> 00:07:02.080
All but one. Mors of House Martell.
He saw in her a strength to match any man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:08.080
including his rivals. After she accepted his&nbsp;
marriage offer, she set fire to her ships.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:15.840
For fifty leagues, the coast was bright as&nbsp;
day, and in the burning light, Princess Nymeria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:22.080
named Mors Martell the Prince of&nbsp;
Dorne, in the style of her people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:31.520
Dorne would be her home or her grave.
For many years, Nymeria and Mors waged war against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:41.120
all rivals. The Jordaynes, Blackmonts, Qorgyles,&nbsp;
and even the mighty House Yronwood. They sent no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:47.920
fewer than six self-styled "kings" to the Wall&nbsp;
in golden chains. After Mors fell in battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:52.960
Nymeria took command of his armies&nbsp;
and united Dorne in two years.
&nbsp;

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.920
She ruled for twenty-seven more, and though&nbsp;
she married again, those husbands were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:05.920
little more than councilors and consorts.&nbsp;
Dorne was Nymeria, and Nymeria was Dorne.
&nbsp;

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:11.840
She survived a dozen attempts on her life, put&nbsp;
down two rebellions, and threw back two invasions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:18.640
And when at last, she died, her eldest child&nbsp;
succeeded her (her daughter, not her son),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:25.840
and Dorne followed her because Nymeria had proven&nbsp;
that women were equal to men, if not better.
&nbsp;

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:30.960
Centuries later, Aegon Targaryen&nbsp;
sought to unite Westeros,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:36.640
as Nymeria had Dorne. The other six kingdoms&nbsp;
fell quickly before his dragons and ambition.
&nbsp;

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:42.640
When his sister-wife, Rhaenys, flew her dragon&nbsp;
south and demanded Dorne's surrender as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:48.880
Princess Meria Martell warned, "I will&nbsp;
not fight you, nor will I kneel to you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:52.160
Dorne has no king. Tell your brother that."
&nbsp;

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:57.040
Rhaenys threatened that the next time the&nbsp;
Targaryens would come with fire and blood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:03.840
Meria replied, "You may burn us,&nbsp;
my lady, but you will not bend us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:13.040
break us or make us bow. This is Dorne; you&nbsp;
are not wanted here. Return at your peril!"
&nbsp;

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:23.280
Rhaenys did, and she died. Her dragon&nbsp;
died. All her soldiers died. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:29.280
her brother, the Conqueror, conceded that&nbsp;
what Nymeria had done, he could not undo.
&nbsp;

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:34.960
Generations later, another&nbsp;
foolish Targaryen invaded Dorne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:43.840
He died as well. Eventually, we did join the Seven&nbsp;
Kingdoms, but when we wanted and on our terms. 
&nbsp;

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:48.400
If dragons could not conquer&nbsp;
us, why should we fear lions?
&nbsp;

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:57.840
"Unbowed, unbent, unbroken." The words of House&nbsp;
Martell.The words of Dorne. Men may forget,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:02.480
but women always remember. When we were divided,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:14.480
Nymeria united us. When we were&nbsp;
invaded, Meria defended us.

